					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-516860#post-1498139</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-516860/strangers-of-site-17:105#post-1498139</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 03 Jul 2012 23:15:52 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1361261</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This tale is in response a challenge issued by Roget in the forums: Write a tale about two SCPs you despise, and portray them in a positive light. For me, this is without question <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-105">SCP-105</a> and <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-343">SCP-343</a>. Today's half concerns 105; tomorrow's features SCP-343. I was originally going to write it all up at once, but it proved to be a little long.</p> <p>Whether or not this is &quot;a positive light&quot;, I can't say for sure. It's positive to me in the sense that it takes what I find to be the interesting part of 105 and focuses on it. Hope people enjoy it.</p> <p>EDIT: Because I split this up into two parts, I now realize that this could be construed to be a tale killing off an SCP I don't like. This is not at all my intention, and there's more to the story, which I will post tomorrow.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
